    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nFollowing the implementation of DEC mode 2031 support in #31999, Neovim's `:terminal` correctly sends theme update reports (`\\x1b[?997;1n` / `\\x1b[?997;2n`) when `vim.o.background` changes.\n\nHowever, if an application running inside `:terminal` enables mode 2031 via `CSI ? 2031 h` at startup, Neovim does not send an initial report of the current theme state. Neovim only emits `terminal_notify_theme()` if `'background'` actively transitions later in `did_set_background`.\n\nBecause modern TUIs (such as those using Charm's Bubble Tea / Lip Gloss) subscribe to mode 2031 on bootstrap, they start with an unconfirmed state and never receive a dark-mode confirmation unless the host theme actively changes while the TUI is running.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nWhen `VTERM_PROP_THEMEUPDATES` is enabled for a terminal buffer in `src/nvim/terminal.c`, immediately dispatch an initial `terminal_notify_theme()` report with the current state:\n\n```c\ncase VTERM_PROP_THEMEUPDATES:\n  term->theme_updates = val->boolean;\n  if (val->boolean) {\n    terminal_notify_theme(term, (*p_bg == 'd'));\n  }\n  break;\n```\n\nThis provides child processes with the current color scheme immediately upon subscribing without having to wait for a subsequent theme change or rely on asynchronous OSC 11 roundtrips.",
    "closed_at": "2026-11-01T18:08:40Z",
